\"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Is the spin wheel actually random, or could it favour certain students?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Every spin calls your browser's Web Cryptography API (window.crypto.getRandomValues) with rejection sampling, giving each active student an exact equal probability with zero operator bias.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Can I use it on an interactive whiteboard or projector?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes — it runs in any Chromebook, tablet, or whiteboard browser with Fullscreen Mode so every student in the back row can read the slices clearly.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"What if a student who's already been picked comes up again?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Toggle Remove Winner After Spin in Settings so chosen names exit the wheel cleanly until every classmate has had a fair turn.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Do I need to rebuild it every lesson?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"No. Click Save Custom Wheel to keep each class period stored locally in your browser's LocalStorage, or bookmark its shareable link for one-click access.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Question\",\n          \"name\": \"Does it suit every age group?\",\n          \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n            \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n            \"text\": \"Yes — younger classes enjoy the visual spin and sound effects, while middle and high school students appreciate visible fairness for partner assignments and presentation orders.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n  