        <h2 id="faq">8. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
            Is the spin wheel actually random, or could it favour certain
            students?<span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-a">
            Every spin pulls unbiased numbers from your browser's Web Cryptography API
            (<code>window.crypto.getRandomValues()</code>) with rejection sampling, so each student holds an exact equal probability before the wheel even starts turning. Our article on
            <a href="/blogs/is-spin-wheel-truly-random" class="ilink-green"
              >whether a digital spin wheel is truly random</a
            >
            explains the mechanics in plain language, useful if a curious
            student or parent ever asks.
          </div>
        </div>

