        <h2 id="conclusion">9. Final Thoughts</h2>
        <p>
          Teaching is demanding enough without adding a tool that needs
          training, a subscription, or a complicated setup. A spin wheel is the
          opposite of that — one of the few genuinely free classroom tools that
          noticeably changes lesson energy for almost no setup cost at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          What makes it work isn't just the randomness — it's the shared,
          visible experience of watching it spin. When the whole class watches
          that wheel slow down together, everyone's attention is on the same
          thing at the same time. That kind of collective focus is genuinely
          hard to manufacture, and it's sitting there, free, in a browser tab.
        </p>
